{{Quote|We need fighting to feed the machine and our profits.''"<br />"''After our attack, the chances of peace will disappear. The Banking Clan, the Trade Federation and the Techno Union will all get their fair share. And then some.|Gume Saam and [[Count]] [[Dooku]]|<ref name="heroes" />}}
'''Gume Saam''' was a [[Gender|male]] [[Ishi Tib]] [[senator]] who represented the [[Techno Union]] in the [[Galactic Republic]] prior to and during the [[Clone Wars]]. During the conflict, he secretly furthered the interests of the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]].

==Biography==
===Representative of the Union===
{{Quote|Gume Saam? He's no fan of the Jedi.|Mace Windu|<ref name="Obi-Wan and Anakin">''[[Choose Your Destiny: An Obi-Wan & Anakin Adventure]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Palpatine_on_balcony.jpg|thumb|left|220px|Saam with Chancellor Palpatine and several other senators]]
Saam was a [[Gender|male]] [[senator]] for the [[Techno Union]]<ref name="heroes" /> in the [[Galactic Senate]], having taken on the role sometime before the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="Obi-Wan and Anakin" /> In [[26 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> [[Jedi]] [[Grand Master]] [[Yoda]], [[Jedi Master]] [[Mace Windu]], and Jedi Master [[Bant Eerin]] launched a [[Rescue of Yoda|fake kidnapping of Yoda]] to test [[Jedi Knight]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Padawan]] [[Anakin Skywalker]], including using a [[squadron]] of [[battle droid]]s, which had been manufactured by the Techno Union, as a diversion. Unaware that it was a test, Kenobi suggested approaching Saam, though Windu noted he was not supportive of the [[Jedi Order]]. Due to this, the Jedi Knight suggested going to the Union headquarters on [[Skako Minor]], though Skywalker realized a [[droid]]'s head also had a non-Union symbol. This sign actually belonged to the [[Nova Crime Syndicate]], which pointed Kenobi and Skywalker to [[the Wheel]] and then [[Glee Anselm]], where they found Yoda and learned it had been a test.<ref name="Obi-Wan and Anakin" />

Following the [[First Battle of Geonosis|Battle]] of [[Geonosis]], Saam was with [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] and several other senators who oversaw the deployment of the newly formed [[Grand Army of the Republic]] from [[Coruscant]].<ref name="Attack of the Clones">{{Film|II}}</ref>

===Clone Wars===
{{Quote|This is a matter not of philosophy. More troops are needed. The Republic cannot afford to let the Separatists gain any more ground!|Gume Saam|<ref name="heroes" />}}
[[File:Military_enhancement_bill.png|thumb|left|250px|Gume Saam with [[Lott Dod]] in the Senate]]
During the Clone Wars, Saam tried to push a [[Republic financial reform bill|bill]] that would deregulate the banks in the [[Galactic Senate|Republic Senate]] while allowing for additional funds for clone troopers, but was rejected due to [[Bail Prestor Organa|Bail Organa]] saying that the Senate should table any emergency bill until it was time to deregulate the banks, which [[Mas Amedda]] supported. Following that session of the senate, Saam spoke with [[InterGalactic Banking Clan|Banking Clan]] Senator [[Nix Card]] and [[Trade Federation]] Senator [[Lott Dod]]. Saam told them that he tried to push the bill through, but Card knew it was unlikely the Senate would deregulate the Banking Clan. Dod thought the problem was [[Naboo]]'s Senator [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] causing Saam to say that she should be taken care of, but the [[Neimoidian]] warned him that killing her was more harder then he thought and the [[Muun]] agreed due to his beliefs on how the Banking Clan and the Trade Federation were about business and not violence and even if Senator Amidala was dead the Senate would not deregulate the Banks so he suggested that Coruscant be attacked to force the Senate to deregulate the Banking Clan. Saam said he liked the plan, but Card insisted no one cared what he thought.<ref name="heroes" />

After the [[Separatist Senate]] voted to open [[Confederate–Republic peace initiative|peace talks]] with the Republic, Saam and his supporters were shocked to hear of this development. Saam said that they needed war to make profits for themselves. They were assured when [[Count]] [[Dooku]] told them that chances of peace would disappear after their [[Bombing of Coruscant's central power distribution grid|attack]]. During the Senate's vote on the peace initiative, Saam and his supporters were surprised that Dooku's attack was late. However, when the power went out due to the [[Infiltrator demolition droid|demolition droids]], all the senators believed they were under attack. Saam then told the Senate that the attack was confirmed to have been carried out by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatists]] and demanded that they pay for what they have done. Thus, the Senate deregulated the banks, pleasing the Ishi Tib and allowing the future of more troops to become a reality.<ref name="heroes" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Gume Saam first appeared in [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']].

Saam was voiced in ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' by [[Phil LaMarr]], also the voice of Senators [[Bail Prestor Organa|Bail Organa]] and [[Orn Free Taa]]. In the credits for "[[Heroes on Both Sides]]," he was mistakenly identified as "Gume '''Sam'''."

